alue":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-23T14:56:59-07:00","id":178263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Laughing Hyena</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/177299-world-of-darkness-fan-nicknames-edition?p=177503#post177503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From <b>Inquest #11, page 89</b> aka &quot;Proof&quot;. Hope the upload attachments work, so this shows up.<br /> Still, nowhere near as bad as the typos in the Scrye Collectible Card Game Checklist and Price Guide for Rage Promos (<i>In both books by the way, 2001 and the 2003 edition)</i>.<br /> <br /> Okay, it didn't show up. So I had to use other means to get this image to show.<br /> <img src=\"http://media.tumblr.com/a7f2a331b949d24d4dfd537ae24820cc/tumblr_inline_n7lkgws2Kd1rwmu7n.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> </div> </div> </div>That wasn't a typo. Inquest did that sort of thing all over the place in their price guide and in the card descriptions.<br /> <br /> Man, back in the day when every single Magic card could fit in the back couple pages of a skinny monthly magazine!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/612-the-cat-came-back","name":"The Cat Came Back","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar612_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-23T15:05:32-07:00","id":178267,"title":"","content":"Mini-Ahroun: a non-ahroun played as a combat monkey exclusively over the auspice duty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-24T01:53:07-07:00","id":178746,"title":"","content":"I once played in a local Mexico City by Night game with one of my friends who loved to roleplay his characters. He was a Brujah Luchador with a very thick Mexican accent, and he would refer to the two Lasombra in his pack as his &quot;LasHOMBRES&quot;, he also would do shots of vitae with a worm in them instead of Tequila (which, at the table, would be in the form of him taking a shot of Tequila with a gummy worm in it). Needless to say, that was one of the funnest games I've been in. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>\u201cAnd those who were seen dancing were thought to be insane by those who could not hear the music.\u201d - Friedrich Nietzsche</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/812-datura","name":"Datura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar812_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-24T04:43:12-07:00","id":178792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Datura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/177299-world-of-darkness-fan-nicknames-edition?p=178746#post178746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I once played in a local Mexico City by Night game with one of my friends who loved to roleplay his characters. He was a Brujah Luchador with a very thick Mexican accent, and he would refer to the two Lasombra in his pack as his &quot;LasHOMBRES&quot;, he also would do shots of vitae with a worm in them instead of Tequila (which, at the table, would be in the form of him taking a shot of Tequila with a gummy worm in it). Needless to say, that was one of the funnest games I've been in.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That might be the stupidest/awesome thing i have ever hear in mah freakin life, give that man extra experience points, an icecream, and get him laid somehow","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T07:52:54-07:00","id":182888,"title":"","content":"After the V:tES card for Enkidu came out one of my friends looked at it and said, &quot;What the hell is that? Some sort of deformed Pokemon?&quot; To which we responded &quot;Yes it's Enkichu, gotta catch 'em all.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1399-lord_boofhead","name":"Lord_Boofhead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1399_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-03T14:03:34-07:00","id":187394,"title":"","content":"Not as funny as some of the other stuff here, but a few of my friends couldn't decide whether or not to call him Samuel &quot;Hate&quot; or Samuel &quot;Height&quot;. To keep the conversation from being derailed I said &quot;just call him Sammy H&quot; and it stuck. Real hard to take him seriously after that, with all the Pulp Fiction references to the tune of Sam &quot;Sammy&quot; Jackson's lines. In fact, the Skinner even dared someone to say what again during a very tense scene. Serious, serious, serious, people bleeding, desperation, don't kill our friend and steal his powers, then bam, out of nowhere. It was great. Killed the mood, but it was worth the laugh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3407-cerushad","name":"Cerushad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3407_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-09T23:22:13-07:00","id":193204,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve always called the Children of Gaia, the \u201cCoggies,\u201d I don\u2019t know if that\u2019s common or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u200b<span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\">Dante \u201cOwns-All-the-Books\u201d Laughing-Coyote<br /> <a href=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/91390940/Werewolf%20the%20Apocalypse%20Reference.xlsx\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf (and Human) Reference Excel Spreadsheet</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/clouddrive/share?s=VoD6R2UDSGwijaft3H4kbM\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img593/9752/w20supporterhiddengarou.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img546/6111/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1765-rderekp","name":"rderekp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T05:28:36-07:00","id":193423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rderekp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/177299-world-of-darkness-fan-nicknames-edition?p=193204#post193204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019ve always called the Children of Gaia, the \u201cCoggies,\u201d I don\u2019t know if that\u2019s common or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very common, I do it too.<br /> <br /> Often the tribe names tend to become shortened, Fangs, GWs, Gnawers, Fenrir,etc. for ease in play. For Black Spiral Dancers, there is BSDs and then there is Dancers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T07:53:59-07:00","id":193607,"title":"","content":"I think I only know the more common ones.<br /> <br /> For the vamps there's fangs, leech, lawyer.<br /> For the weres there's doggies, furries, pets.<br /> For the mages there's pot-heads, wand-wavers, victims.<br /> For the wraiths there's Casper, bed-sheet, former Mage.<br /> For changelings there's faeries, Dancing Bears, sparklers.<br /> <br /> We never had hunters, mummies or demons in the games, they came too late to be added.<br /> <br /> There was one game where we didn't change the name of the Clan, just pronounced it a bit different. We were a large band of Brujah and we were supposed to make a lot of noise to announce our arrival. So someone just started yelling &quot;BA-RUUUUUUUUUUUUUU-HA!&quot; and we all chimed in. It worked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve nei